[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Whitespace Steganography System Requirements
VERSION: 1.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: PARENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-001
TITLE: Language-Agnostic Design
STATEMENT: The system shall be designed and specified in a programming language-agnostic manner, allowing implementation in any programming language that supports Unicode string manipulation and Base64 encoding/decoding operations.
RATIONALE: To ensure the requirements can be implemented across diverse technology stacks and environments, maximizing the system's applicability and portability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-002
TITLE: Invisible Character Steganography Method
STATEMENT: The system shall use invisible Unicode control characters as the steganographic medium, specifically zero-width characters that are not visible when rendered in standard text displays.
RATIONALE: To ensure the encoded messages remain undetectable during normal text viewing and processing, maintaining the covert nature of the steganography.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-003
TITLE: Bidirectional Message Processing
STATEMENT: The system shall provide both encoding and decoding capabilities, allowing messages to be embedded into text and subsequently extracted from encoded text.
RATIONALE: To enable complete steganographic communication workflows where messages can be both concealed and recovered.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-004
TITLE: Unicode Control Character Specifications
STATEMENT: The system shall use the following Unicode control characters for encoding: CONTROL_START: U+2060 (Word Joiner) to mark the beginning of an encoded payload; CONTROL_END: U+2063 (Invisible Separator) to mark the end of an encoded payload; BIT_0: U+200B (Zero Width Space) to represent binary bit value 0; BIT_1: U+200C (Zero Width Non-Joiner) to represent binary bit value 1.
RATIONALE: These specific Unicode characters are chosen because they are invisible when rendered, allowing encoded messages to remain undetectable in normal text viewing contexts.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-005
TITLE: Base64 Encoding Standard
STATEMENT: The system shall use Base64 encoding as specified in RFC 4648 to encode the original message before binary conversion.
RATIONALE: Base64 encoding ensures that any message content (including binary data) can be safely represented as ASCII characters, which can then be converted to binary format for steganographic encoding.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-006
TITLE: Binary Representation Format
STATEMENT: The system shall represent each Base64-encoded character as an 8-bit binary value, with bits ordered from most significant bit (MSB) to least significant bit (LSB).
RATIONALE: Standard 8-bit byte representation ensures consistent encoding and decoding across different platforms and character encodings.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-007
TITLE: Control Marker Positioning
STATEMENT: The encoded payload shall be wrapped with CONTROL_START immediately before the first bit character and CONTROL_END immediately after the last bit character, with no intervening characters between the markers and the payload.
RATIONALE: Precise marker positioning ensures reliable payload extraction during decoding operations.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-008
TITLE: Message Encoding Capability
STATEMENT: The system shall encode an input message string into a steganographic representation using invisible Unicode control characters.
RATIONALE: Encoding is a fundamental operation required to conceal messages within text.
PARENT: REQ-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-009
TITLE: UTF-8 Message Encoding
STATEMENT: The system shall encode the input message to UTF-8 byte sequence before applying Base64 encoding.
RATIONALE: UTF-8 encoding ensures that messages containing any Unicode characters can be properly processed, supporting international text and emoji characters.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-010
TITLE: Base64 Encoding Application
STATEMENT: The system shall apply Base64 encoding to the UTF-8 encoded message bytes to produce a Base64-encoded string.
RATIONALE: Base64 encoding converts arbitrary byte sequences into a safe ASCII representation that can be reliably converted to binary format.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-011
TITLE: Binary Conversion
STATEMENT: The system shall convert each character in the Base64-encoded string to its 8-bit binary representation, producing a sequence of binary digits (0s and 1s).
RATIONALE: Binary representation is necessary to map message data to individual bit values that can be encoded as invisible characters.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-012
TITLE: Bit-to-Character Mapping
STATEMENT: The system shall map each binary digit to its corresponding invisible Unicode character, where bit value 0 maps to BIT_0 (U+200B) and bit value 1 maps to BIT_1 (U+200C).
RATIONALE: This mapping creates the steganographic payload that can be embedded invisibly within text.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-013
TITLE: Control Marker Wrapping
STATEMENT: The system shall wrap the sequence of bit-encoded invisible characters with CONTROL_START (U+2060) at the beginning and CONTROL_END (U+2063) at the end to form the complete encoded payload.
RATIONALE: Control markers enable the decoder to identify and extract the encoded payload from text that may contain other content.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-014
TITLE: Carrier Text Embedding Support
STATEMENT: The system shall support optional embedding of the encoded message within a carrier text string, where the encoded payload is inserted after the first character of the carrier text.
RATIONALE: Carrier text embedding allows encoded messages to be hidden within seemingly normal text, enhancing the steganographic concealment.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-015
TITLE: Standalone Encoding Mode
STATEMENT: The system shall support encoding a message without carrier text, producing a string containing only the control markers and encoded payload.
RATIONALE: Standalone encoding mode provides flexibility for use cases where carrier text is not needed or will be added separately.
PARENT: REQ-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-016
TITLE: Message Decoding Capability
STATEMENT: The system shall decode a steganographically encoded string to recover the original message.
RATIONALE: Decoding is a fundamental operation required to extract concealed messages from encoded text.
PARENT: REQ-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-017
TITLE: Control Marker Detection
STATEMENT: The system shall detect the presence of CONTROL_START and CONTROL_END markers within the input string to identify the encoded payload boundaries.
RATIONALE: Marker detection is necessary to locate and extract the encoded payload from text that may contain additional content.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-018
TITLE: Payload Extraction
STATEMENT: The system shall extract the sequence of invisible characters located between the CONTROL_START and CONTROL_END markers, excluding the markers themselves from the payload.
RATIONALE: Accurate payload extraction is required to obtain the bit-encoded data for subsequent decoding operations.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-019
TITLE: Character-to-Bit Conversion
STATEMENT: The system shall convert each invisible character in the extracted payload to its corresponding binary digit, where BIT_0 (U+200B) maps to bit value 0 and BIT_1 (U+200C) maps to bit value 1.
RATIONALE: This conversion reverses the encoding process, reconstructing the binary representation of the Base64-encoded message.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-020
TITLE: Binary-to-Byte Conversion
STATEMENT: The system shall group the sequence of binary digits into 8-bit bytes, converting each 8-bit group from binary representation to its corresponding byte value.
RATIONALE: Byte reconstruction is necessary to convert the binary bit sequence back into character data for Base64 decoding.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-021
TITLE: Base64 Decoding
STATEMENT: The system shall apply Base64 decoding to the reconstructed byte sequence to recover the original UTF-8 encoded message bytes.
RATIONALE: Base64 decoding reverses the Base64 encoding applied during the encoding process, recovering the original message bytes.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-022
TITLE: UTF-8 Message Decoding
STATEMENT: The system shall decode the UTF-8 byte sequence to produce the original message string.
RATIONALE: UTF-8 decoding recovers the original message text from the byte representation, completing the decoding process.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-023
TITLE: Round-Trip Integrity
STATEMENT: The system shall ensure that decoding an encoded message produces the exact original message, with no data loss or corruption.
RATIONALE: Round-trip integrity is essential for reliable steganographic communication, ensuring messages can be accurately recovered.
PARENT: REQ-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-024
TITLE: Missing Start Marker Detection
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when the CONTROL_START marker is absent from the input string during decoding operations and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: Missing start markers indicate invalid or corrupted encoded data, requiring appropriate error handling to prevent incorrect decoding results.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-025
TITLE: Missing End Marker Detection
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when the CONTROL_END marker is absent from the input string during decoding operations and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: Missing end markers indicate incomplete or corrupted encoded data, requiring appropriate error handling to prevent incorrect decoding results.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-026
TITLE: Invalid Payload Character Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when the extracted payload contains characters other than BIT_0 (U+200B) and BIT_1 (U+200C) and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: Invalid characters in the payload indicate corrupted or malformed encoded data, requiring error detection to maintain decoding reliability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-027
TITLE: Base64 Decoding Failure Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when Base64 decoding fails due to invalid Base64 data and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: Base64 decoding failures indicate corrupted payload data or encoding errors, requiring appropriate error handling.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-028
TITLE: UTF-8 Decoding Failure Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when UTF-8 decoding fails due to invalid UTF-8 byte sequences and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: UTF-8 decoding failures indicate corrupted message data, requiring appropriate error handling to prevent invalid output.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-029
TITLE: Incomplete Payload Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall detect when the extracted payload does not contain a complete number of 8-bit bytes (i.e., the bit count is not divisible by 8) and handle this condition as an error.
RATIONALE: Incomplete payloads indicate truncated or corrupted encoded data, requiring error detection to prevent incorrect decoding.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-030
TITLE: Error Reporting
STATEMENT: The system shall report decoding errors in a manner that clearly indicates the nature of the failure, allowing calling code to distinguish between different error conditions.
RATIONALE: Clear error reporting enables proper error handling in applications using the steganography system, improving system reliability and debuggability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-031
TITLE: Encoding Function Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide an encoding function that accepts a message string as input and returns an encoded string containing the steganographic representation of the message.
RATIONALE: A well-defined encoding interface enables integration of the steganography system into various applications and use cases.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-032
TITLE: Encoding Function with Carrier Text
STATEMENT: The system shall provide an encoding function variant that accepts both a message string and an optional carrier text string, returning a string containing the carrier text with the encoded message embedded within it.
RATIONALE: Support for carrier text embedding provides enhanced steganographic concealment capabilities.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-033
TITLE: Decoding Function Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide a decoding function that accepts an encoded string as input and returns the decoded message string, or raises an error if decoding fails.
RATIONALE: A well-defined decoding interface enables reliable message extraction from encoded text.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-034
TITLE: String Input/Output Format
STATEMENT: All interface functions shall accept and return string data types that support Unicode character representation, capable of handling the invisible Unicode control characters used for encoding.
RATIONALE: Unicode string support is essential for handling the invisible control characters that form the basis of the steganographic encoding.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-035
TITLE: Empty Input Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall handle empty message strings as valid input for encoding operations, producing an encoded string containing only the control markers with an empty payload.
RATIONALE: Supporting empty inputs provides interface consistency and enables edge case handling in applications.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-036
TITLE: Empty Carrier Text Handling
STATEMENT: The system shall handle empty carrier text strings as valid input, producing encoded output equivalent to encoding without carrier text.
RATIONALE: Supporting empty carrier text provides interface flexibility, allowing applications to conditionally include carrier text.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-037
TITLE: Programming Language Independence
STATEMENT: The system specification shall be independent of any specific programming language, allowing implementation in any language that supports Unicode string operations and Base64 encoding/decoding.
RATIONALE: Language independence ensures the requirements can be implemented across diverse technology stacks, maximizing system applicability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-038
TITLE: Unicode Character Encoding Support
STATEMENT: The system shall support Unicode character encoding (specifically UTF-8) for both input messages and encoded output, enabling support for international text, emoji, and other Unicode characters.
RATIONALE: Unicode support ensures the system can handle messages containing any text content, not limited to ASCII characters.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-039
TITLE: Message Size Scalability
STATEMENT: The system shall support encoding and decoding messages of arbitrary size, limited only by the underlying platform's string handling capabilities and memory constraints.
RATIONALE: Scalability ensures the system can handle messages ranging from short text to large documents, accommodating diverse use cases.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-040
TITLE: Stealthiness Requirement
STATEMENT: The encoded messages shall be visually imperceptible when rendered in standard text displays, appearing identical to unencoded text or carrier text.
RATIONALE: Visual imperceptibility is fundamental to steganography, ensuring encoded messages remain undetectable during normal text viewing.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-041
TITLE: Encoding Determinism
STATEMENT: The system shall produce identical encoded output when encoding the same message with the same carrier text, ensuring deterministic encoding behavior.
RATIONALE: Deterministic encoding enables reliable testing, verification, and predictable system behavior across different implementations and executions.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-042
TITLE: Decoding Robustness
STATEMENT: The system shall successfully decode any valid encoded string produced by the encoding function, ensuring complete round-trip compatibility.
RATIONALE: Decoding robustness ensures that encoded messages can be reliably recovered, maintaining the integrity of the steganographic communication channel.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-043
TITLE: Performance Efficiency
STATEMENT: The system shall perform encoding and decoding operations efficiently, with computational complexity that scales linearly with message size.
RATIONALE: Linear time complexity ensures the system remains practical for real-world use cases, handling messages of various sizes without excessive performance degradation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-044
TITLE: Memory Efficiency
STATEMENT: The system shall operate with memory usage that scales linearly with input message size, avoiding excessive memory overhead during encoding and decoding operations.
RATIONALE: Efficient memory usage ensures the system can operate within reasonable resource constraints, supporting deployment in resource-limited environments.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-045
TITLE: Optional Password-Based Encryption
STATEMENT: The system shall support optional password-based encryption of messages before Base64 encoding, using XOR cipher with a password-derived key.
RATIONALE: Password protection adds an additional layer of security to encoded messages, ensuring that only parties with the correct password can decode the hidden content.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-046
TITLE: Password Key Derivation
STATEMENT: The system shall derive an encryption key from the password by repeating the password bytes cyclically to match the length of the message UTF-8 byte sequence.
RATIONALE: Cyclic key repetition provides a simple and deterministic key derivation method that works with passwords of any length while maintaining backward compatibility when no password is provided.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-047
TITLE: XOR Encryption Process
STATEMENT: The system shall apply XOR encryption to each UTF-8 byte of the message with the corresponding byte from the password-derived key before applying Base64 encoding.
RATIONALE: XOR encryption is a symmetric cipher that allows the same password to both encrypt and decrypt the message, and it operates on the plaintext before Base64 encoding to ensure the carrier text appears normal.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-048
TITLE: XOR Decryption Process
STATEMENT: The system shall apply XOR decryption to the Base64-decoded bytes using the same password-derived key to recover the original message.
RATIONALE: XOR decryption reverses the encryption process, recovering the original message when the correct password is provided.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-049
TITLE: Password Backward Compatibility
STATEMENT: The system shall maintain backward compatibility with existing encoded messages by making the password parameter optional, allowing encoding and decoding without passwords to function as before.
RATIONALE: Backward compatibility ensures that existing encoded messages continue to work without modification, preserving the usability of the system across version updates.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-050
TITLE: Password Interface Support
STATEMENT: The system shall provide encoding and decoding functions that accept an optional password parameter, allowing applications to choose whether to use password protection.
RATIONALE: Optional password support provides flexibility for applications that may or may not require password protection, accommodating diverse use cases and security requirements.

